<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="DevDeck.App.Views.Gauge">

  <!-- A ring gauge. Two ellipses: a full-circle track, and the reading drawn on top of it as a
       single dash whose length is the percentage.

       Dashes rather than an Arc, deliberately. Avalonia's Arc has StartAngle and SweepAngle, and
       measured off a screenshot a 28% arc sat straddling twelve o'clock rather than starting
       there, in both sweep directions. A dashed ellipse is plain arithmetic instead - the
       circumference is pi x diameter, a dash length is a multiple of the stroke width - and the
       -90 degree rotation below is what puts the start of the dash at twelve. -->

  <Panel>
    <Ellipse Name="Track"
             Stroke="{DynamicResource Track}"
             HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />

    <Ellipse Name="Progress"
             HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
             StrokeLineCap="Round"
             RenderTransform="rotate(-90deg)"
             RenderTransformOrigin="50%,50%" />

    <!-- Nothing in the middle, deliberately. An earlier cut had a ContentPresenter here bound to
         $parent[UserControl].Content, so a caller could drop a figure into the hole - but a
         UserControl's Content is its own root Panel, so the gauge was asking to host itself. It
         crashed the moment a window containing one was shown.

         Callers that want something in the middle layer it over the gauge in their own Panel,
         which needs no API here and cannot recurse. -->
  </Panel>
</UserControl>
